1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,960
On the twelfth of November 2025,

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,400
the United States Mint struck

3
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:07,960
its last cent for circulation.

4
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:11,400
A year on, the cent is still legal tender.

5
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:14,920
But by July 2026, 20 states had passed laws

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,280
letting shops round a cash

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,440
total to the nearest five cents.

8
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,000
In September, Congress passed the Common Cents

9
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:24,453
Act, which would allow the same across the country.

10
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:28,960
The face value of the cent is being rounded away.

11
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:30,960
That same September, copper traded

12
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,100
higher in London than it ever had before.

13
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,620
A cent struck before the switch

14
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:39,220
to zinc in 1982 is 95% copper.

15
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,980
At that peak, the metal in one

16
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:44,140
was worth more than four cents.

17
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:45,740
The coin says one.

18
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:50,180
For most of 20 years, its copper has said more.

19
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,940
That gap, between what the state

20
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:54,207
decrees and what the metal holds,

21
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:57,180
is where CENTS begins.

22
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:59,260
Rutherford Chang removed 10,000

23
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:00,900
copper cents from circulation,

24
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:02,500
and photographed each one,

25
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:04,393
front and back.

26
00:01:04,447 --> 00:01:06,860
He melted them into a single block of copper,

27
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,873
31 kilograms.

28
00:01:09,927 --> 00:01:12,140
In March 2024, the image of each

29
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,753
front was inscribed on its own satoshi.

30
00:01:15,807 --> 00:01:17,660
A Cent is a unit of currency,

31
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,113
a quantity of copper,

32
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:20,233
part of a sculpture,

33
00:01:20,287 --> 00:01:22,700
a photograph, and a Bitcoin inscription.

34
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:25,727
Each is valued by a different measure.

35
00:01:25,753 --> 00:01:27,420
And the measures keep moving.

36
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:28,860
Over two years of voting,

37
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,100
collectors named the marks

38
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,900
that circulation left on them:

39
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:36,820
verdigris, obsidian, fingerprints, ghost.

40
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,380
The cent is leaving the till.

41
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,580
In CENTS, what a cent is worth

42
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,100
is still being decided.

